# Agatha's Soul Cauldron: "{T}: Exile target card from a graveyard. When a creature card is exiled this way, put a +1/+1
# counter on target creature you control." Bot2 discards its newest card to hand size each turn: an Ornithopter on turn 2,
# an Island on turn 4, an Ornithopter on turn 6. Turn 3: the Cauldron exiles the creature card while Bot1 controls no
# creature (the Cauldron is not one), so the reflexive trigger has no target and nothing happens (CR 603.3d). Turn 5, with
# Bot1's Ornithopter out: it exiles the Island, not a creature card, so no counter. Turn 7: a creature card, and the
# counter goes on the Ornithopter (the positive control for both refusals).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Agatha's Soul Cauldron
Ornithopter
Mountain x3
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Ornithopter
Island
Ornithopter
Island x6

